  "explanation": {
    "short": "At the start of a word, i before another vowel is said like \"y\" in \"yes\": iam is yahm, ianua is YAH-noo-ah. The letter j, where it is written, is the same sound. A double letter, as in terra, is held a little longer.",
    "more": "Iesus, with this same sound, is YEH-soos. The double r in terra is rolled and held: TER-rah, not TEH-rah."
  },
